WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.899
Designing molecules that optimize a property,

00:00:02.979 --> 00:00:07.996
like binding tightly to a viral protein, is a
central goal in drug discovery,

00:00:08.076 --> 00:00:09.386
yet hard to automate.

00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:13.093
The chemical space is discrete and astronomically large,

00:00:13.173 --> 00:00:15.012
making exploration difficult,

00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:19.315
and compressing a molecule's atom-and-bond graph
into a faithful,

00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:22.360
learnable representation is itself nontrivial.
